Frontier is an independent video game developer and publisher, crafting immersive gaming experiences with fun gameplay and unparalleled artistic quality. Renowned for its iconic creative management simulation games, Frontier captivates players worldwide with immersive and authentic game worlds. The modern studio is located in the vibrant technology hub of Cambridge (UK). The talented team at Frontier are dedicated to nurturing our existing portfolio and delivering our exciting future roadmap.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
This role is offered on a full in-studio basis or a hybrid basis (minimum 3 days per week in the studio). We can provide a comprehensive relocation support package as part of any offer, should you need to relocate.&nbsp;

WHAT'S THE ROLE?


We’re looking for a Senior Game Designer to join our team and bring their expertise in game design to help create engaging, player first experiences for our creative management simulation titles.&nbsp;


As a Senior Game Designer, you will take ownership of significant game features, and work collaboratively with other disciplines to turn great ideas into compelling experiences that players love.&nbsp;

WHAT YOU'LL BE DOING


Design and iteration of complex game features
Implementing and refining game content using in-house tools
Building alignment and understanding of game features with clear verbal and written communication
Ensuring games systems are balanced using analytical methods and incorporating game telemetry
Driving quality using playtests, player feedback, QA reporting, and your own insights&nbsp;


WHAT YOU'LL BRING


Deep game knowledge across a range of genres
Strong commercial game design experience throughout the product lifecycle on PC &amp; console
Solid understanding of player psychology and gamer motivations
Excellent communications skills; ability to present your ideas clearly in verbal and written form
Effective collaboration with both team members and external stakeholders&nbsp;


BONUS IF YOU HAVE



Good knowledge of simulation and management games
Knowledge of UI/UX design principles
Experience developing tutorials and first-time user flows
Experience in coaching and mentoring team members&nbsp;



WHAT WE CAN OFFER YOU
You will work with talented and passionate people to support, develop or publish our sophisticated and enduring games, in a creative, collaborative and inclusive environment. We love what we do, and we work hard to provide outstanding experiences for our players.&nbsp;Wellbeing is a big focus at Frontier, and we are continually evolving how we can support our people. We encourage a healthy work/life balance and provide a range of wellbeing activities, initiatives and sessions to support both mental and physical health.&nbsp;&nbsp;We offer a competitive salary and benefits package, which includes a success-based annual bonus, share option schemes, life assurance, private family healthcare, flexitime working hours, enhanced maternity/paternity leave, in-house subsidised catering, support with relocation, a Cycle to Work scheme, free bike servicing, and social activities and events.&nbsp;We strive to create an environment where everyone can fully demonstrate their capability and potential. If you therefore need any reasonable adjustments to support you during the recruitment process, please speak to your Talent Acquisition representative.&nbsp;&nbsp;For queries, please email: -----Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

