&lt;h3&gt;🧡 About Alma&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Alma, we believe sustainable commerce depends on fair, well-balanced trade. Because finance plays a pivotal role in business, our mission is to put it back in its rightful place, serving merchants and consumers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our installment and deferred payment solutions help merchants boost sales by 20% or more, increase customer loyalty, and deliver a seamless shopping experience, without encouraging bad debt.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the buy now pay later leader in France and active in 10 European countries, we&#39;ve empowered more than 25,000 merchants and 10 million consumers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With 380+ Almakers and €100M+ ARR, Alma is scaling rapidly across Europe as a member of the Next40, and we&#39;re just getting started!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;👐 About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Revenue at Alma covers the entire customer lifecycle, from lead generation to churn. It brings together Marketing, Partnerships, Sales and Account Management, representing more than 100 talented professionals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Revenue Operations plays a key role in helping these teams work together around shared goals, reliable data and efficient processes. The team supports Revenue leaders in improving performance, making better decisions and scaling the organisation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is a permanent contract, based in Paris, with 2 days of remote work per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/in/basil-lizotte-aa155182&quot;&gt;Basil Lizotte&lt;/a&gt;, and work closely with Revenue teams, the Central Data Team, Ops &amp;amp; Risk, Product and Tech.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;💼 About the job&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Business Analyst, Revenue Operations, you will create strategic insights that help Alma&#39;s Revenue teams understand their performance, identify growth opportunities and improve their speed and efficiency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work at the intersection of data, business and strategy, turning complex questions into clear recommendations and practical tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Build reliable data foundations for Revenue&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and evolve business-facing data models by combining relevant CRM, revenue and operational data sources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve and maintain existing models and contribute to reliable end-to-end data pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Turn business questions into strategic insights&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse Alma&#39;s target markets, market share, market dynamics and the key drivers behind commercial wins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design ad hoc tools and models to help Revenue teams answer tactical business questions and make faster decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Improve performance monitoring and revenue growth&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage dashboards, KPIs and revenue forecasts so teams and leadership can monitor business health and progress against their goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Revenue leaders in setting the right targets, understanding growth dynamics and prioritising their roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Drive data excellence across Revenue&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote data-informed ways of working across Marketing, Partnerships, Sales and Account Management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with the Central Data Team to maintain high standards of data quality and consistency across the organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;🧰 You will work with&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SQL, Looker, LookML, Claude Code, Python, dbt, BigQuery, GCP, Rudderstack, Segment, Salesforce&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;🧩 About you&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;To succeed in this job&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong SQL skills and are comfortable working with large datasets, raw CRM data and revenue-related information, including Salesforce data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience building business-facing data models, dashboards, forecasts or performance analyses from the initial question through to clear recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can define relevant KPIs, assess business impact and communicate complex analysis in a clear and actionable way to different stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have approximately 4 to 7 years of experience in data analysis, business analysis or a similar role, ideally in a fast-growing technology or fintech environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;And it will be nice if you also&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience with Looker and LookML.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable with Python and modern data tools such as dbt, BigQuery or GCP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have worked with tracking tools such as Rudderstack or Segment, as well as experimentation methodologies such as A/B testing, significance testing and causal analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are curious about AI-assisted tools and are interested in using tools such as Claude Code in your daily workflow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Don&#39;t meet every single requirement? At Alma, we believe great hires come from diverse paths. If this role excites you, we encourage you to apply. We value potential, curiosity and the ability to grow as much as experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;🧘 Your Alma experience&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;The culture&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Alma, collective intelligence is at the heart of the way we work. We are building an international company in a fast-growing environment, where people are encouraged to take ownership, share ideas and learn from one another.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have access to our Learning &amp;amp; Development Platform, regular feedback and opportunities to develop your expertise and career path. As Alma continues to grow across Europe, you will have the opportunity to work with colleagues from different teams, countries and areas of expertise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to building a fair and inclusive workplace. We monitor our gender equality index and remain committed to pay equity, transparency and equal opportunities across the organisation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;The role itself&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you join Alma, you will be able to grow and have an impact by:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influencing strategic decisions across the full Revenue organisation, from lead generation to churn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Combining analytical depth, business understanding and direct exposure to senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Helping Revenue teams build a stronger data culture and create more efficient ways of working as Alma scales across Europe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;🤑 Compensation &amp;amp; benefits&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competitive salary&lt;/strong&gt; based on 12 months&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Profit-sharing and employee savings plan&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Health insurance&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;strong&gt;100%&lt;/strong&gt; covered by Alma, including family package&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Disability insurance&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;strong&gt;100%&lt;/strong&gt; covered by Alma&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sport&lt;/strong&gt;: partnerships with &lt;strong&gt;Gymlib&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;ClassPass&lt;/strong&gt;, or &lt;strong&gt;€30/month&lt;/strong&gt; reimbursement for your sports activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maternity/paternity leave&lt;/strong&gt;: salary maintained at 100% during leave, with no seniority requirement. Return to work at a 4/5 schedule paid at 100% for 8 weeks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sustainable Mobility Package (FMD)&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;strong&gt;€544.80/year&lt;/strong&gt;, excluding full-remote contracts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Meal vouchers&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;strong&gt;€10/day&lt;/strong&gt;, 50% covered by Alma&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mental health&lt;/strong&gt;: free access to the MindDay platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paid time off&lt;/strong&gt;: 25 days per year, plus additional paid leave granted to employees on executive contracts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to our &lt;strong&gt;Learning &amp;amp; Development Platform&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2 weeks of full remote work possible per year&lt;/strong&gt; during the summer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;🎯 Interview process&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Video screen with Lydia a Talent Acquisition team member&lt;/strong&gt; to discuss your background, motivation and the role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience interview with Basil Lizotte or/and Gaspard Zha&lt;/strong&gt;, lasting 45 minutes, to discuss the role, the team and your experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Home assignment and case study&lt;/strong&gt;, lasting 1 hour, with members team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On-site team fit interview&lt;/strong&gt;, lasting 30 minutes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On-site N+2 interview&lt;/strong&gt; with Antoine de la Rivière, lasting 30 minutes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reference check&lt;/strong&gt; with at least two professional references.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;🌍 Diversity &amp;amp; Inclusion&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Alma, we believe that diversity fuels innovation and makes our community stronger. We are committed to building a workplace where every person feels seen, respected, and empowered to do their best work, whatever their gender, background, ethnicity, age, sexual orientation, religion, disability or lived experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an equal opportunity employer, we welcome applicants from all walks of life, and all employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit and business needs.&lt;/p&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in France on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brief info about Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Our mission is to make second-hand the first choice, and we&#39;re looking for people who want to help us get there. Every day, we work together to help our members buy and sell pre-loved clothing and lifestyle items, giving each piece a second life – or even a third. &lt;br&gt;The Vinted Group is made up of three business units that support this mission:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/marketplace&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Vinted Marketplace&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; is Europe’s leading platform for second-hand fashion and a go-to destination for all kinds of pre-loved items, with a growing range of categories. Our platform connects millions of members across 20+ markets, helping great items find a new life.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedgo&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Go&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; enhances the shipping experience with a vast network of over 500,000 pick-up and drop-off points, partnering with more than 60 carriers across Europe, with added services like item verification for peace of mind on high-value pieces.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedpay&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Pay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is the newest part of the Vinted Group, dedicated to bringing secure, reliable payments to buyers and sellers across Europe. Seamlessly integrated into the Vinted app, it helps keep every transaction safe, efficient, and easy for our members.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2008 in Lithuania, Vinted began as a way for friends to find new homes for clothes they no longer needed. In 2019, we became Lithuania&#39;s first unicorn! Today, our headquarters remain in Vilnius, and we&#39;ve grown with offices across Europe, supported by a team of over 2,000 people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Missions and activities of the position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Project phase – owner&#39;s engineer for Maintenance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Maintenance in every phase of new equipment projects (starting with the MRS1 cross-belt sorter), from design reviews to FAT, SAT, commissioning and ramp-up. For the sorter, whose design is already set, take over the installed system and optimise it after go-live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work side by side with the OEM / integrator engineers: collect technical knowledge, challenge design choices, maintainability, access, spare-part strategy and the proposed maintenance plan before they are frozen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and verify the Maintenance acceptance criteria (documentation, training, spare parts, safety, availability targets). The Maintenance sign-off is mandatory: no handover to operations without it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and drive to closure the technical punch list and warranty issues raised during commissioning and the warranty period.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Technical file &amp;amp; spare parts&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and own the equipment technical file: as-built electrical and mechanical drawings, PLC and software versions, parameter backups, network architecture, safety documentation, OEM manuals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create the asset hierarchy and criticality analysis in the CMMS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the critical spare-parts list (references, min/max stock, lead times) and keep it up to date.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduce dependency on the OEM: identify and qualify second-source suppliers for critical parts, run compatibility tests and document equivalences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Propose spare-parts and supplier decisions to the Maintenance Manager; after an initial period, take these decisions autonomously within agreed limits, with the Maintenance Manager&#39;s validation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Maintenance strategy &amp;amp; procedures&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and maintain preventive maintenance plans, corrective procedures and troubleshooting guides for the equipment family, based on OEM data, FMEA and field experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor equipment performance (availability, MTBF, MTTR, top failure modes), lead root-cause analysis on recurring or major failures and implement permanent corrective actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenge the original design when needed and drive engineering changes: retrofits, drive and firmware updates, software or parameter optimisation, with the OEM and internal stakeholders.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Training &amp;amp; technical support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train the operational maintenance team (technicians and operatives) on the equipment, its software/HMI and the troubleshooting procedures; validate their autonomy level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the level-2 / level-3 technical expert for the equipment family on site and remotely, across sites.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5. Escalation, vendor &amp;amp; SLA management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own technical escalations through to resolution: with the Tetris team (Vinted&#39;s internal tools and sorting logic) when the issue is on the software or data side, and with OEM / integrator support (SAV) when it is on the equipment side.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the diagnosis that tells which side an issue comes from (equipment, controls, Vinted software), with facts and data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work within the after-sales and maintenance agreements already in place with OEMs: make the most of them day to day, monitor performance against SLAs and warranty terms, feed lessons learned into future renewals, and provide the technical evidence to the program managers, who own the contractual relationship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and lead technical review meetings with OEMs and integrators.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;6. Safety &amp;amp; compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the equipment and its maintenance comply with machine safety requirements (CE marking, safety functions, lock-out/tag-out) and site H&amp;amp;S standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support safety audits and regulatory inspections, and drive the resulting corrective actions to completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Occasional responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of additional equipment families (e.g. conveyors, AMR fleets, Monk lines) once the cross-belt is stable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support pre-project technical due diligence on new equipment (specifications, vendor benchmarks, maintainability review).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in the hiring and onboarding of maintenance technicians and future engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interests, constraints, difficulties of the position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High-visibility role on new strategic automation investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Site-based in an operational warehouse, with regular presence on the shop floor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular travel to MRS1, OEM premises (FAT) and other Vinted Go sites, especially during commissioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Day-based role, no on-call. Flexibility needed during commissioning, ramp-up and major incidents (possible early, late or weekend work).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Needs to influence without authority: OEMs, integrators, IT and program management teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge &amp;amp; experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineering degree (Master&#39;s / Bac+5) in automation, electrical, mechatronics or industrial engineering, or Bac+2/3 with equivalent proven experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 3 years&#39; experience, ideally 5 or more, as Equipment Engineer, Automation Engineer, Tool Owner or Maintenance/Reliability Engineer in a highly automated environment: parcel sortation and intralogistics, airport baggage handling, logistics or other automated industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automation background required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven involvement in at least one industrial equipment project from FAT/SAT to ramp-up, working with OEMs or integrators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to read and diagnose complete PLC and HMI programs (Siemens TIA Portal and/or Rockwell, Beckhoff) and to make controlled modifications; industrial networks (Profinet, Profibus, EtherCAT, Ethernet/IP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drives (parameters, firmware), servo motors, sensors, scanners / DWS, pneumatics; reading electrical and mechanical schematics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retrofit experience and component qualification (equivalence, compatibility testing)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Safety PLCs and machine safety functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of the interfaces between equipment controls, SCADA/WCS and IT systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reliability methods: FMEA, RCA (5 Why, Ishikawa, 8D), criticality analysis; CMMS and PM planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sortation equipment experience (cross-belt, tilt-tray, shoe sorters) is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;French electrical certification (habilitation électrique BR / B2V / BC) or ability to obtain it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent French and professional English (OEMs and the Vinted Go network work in English).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Behavioural skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ownership: treats the equipment as their own, from design to end of life.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to challenge OEM and integrator engineers constructively, with facts and data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structured and disciplined in documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good teacher: enjoys transferring knowledge to technicians.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calm and solution-oriented under production pressure; strong safety mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;Please note: the main tasks and skills identified and noted in the function described above may need to evolve depending on the constraints and organisation specific to the company and its environment. They are, therefore, indicative and not contractual.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Working at Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Individual learning budget&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Each year, you’ll be given a learning budget (starting at €3,000), and a total of up to 10 working days over a 2-year period to support your personal and professional development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome applications from everybody, regardless of your background, identity, or life experiences. Job openings come with guides, not checklists. If you’re excited about a role, but don’t identify with every point in the ‘About you’ section, apply anyway – you might still be the perfect match!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The annual gross salary range for this position is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€45.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€60.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in France on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join Our Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a dynamic and customer-focused &lt;strong&gt;Solutions Consultant&lt;/strong&gt; to join our Commercial team in Zurich. This role is ideal for a professional who enjoys combining business insight with technical expertise to help clients solve complex challenges. As a key partner to our Sales, Product, and Operations teams, you will play a critical role in designing tailored solutions, accelerating sales cycles, and ensuring successful customer outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct discovery sessions with prospective clients to understand business processes, challenges, and technical requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex client needs into effective solution designs and technical specifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and present tailored solutions leveraging our product capabilities and integration options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver compelling product demonstrations, presentations, and proof-of-concept workshops for clients and stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the sales team as a technical and functional expert throughout the sales cycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and contribute to RFI and RFP responses, ensuring accuracy and alignment with customer expectations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide effort estimations and implementation guidance for proposed solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Product Development, Operations, and Implementation teams to ensure solution feasibility and successful delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather customer feedback and market insights to support product innovation and strategic decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop sales enablement materials, technical documentation, and case studies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum Bachelor&#39;s degree in Business, Logistics/Supply Chain Management, Computer Science, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience as a Solutions Consultant, Business Implementations, Presales Engineer, Solution Architect, or a similar customer-facing role within enterprise software, SaaS based environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of supply chain management, logistics, or related industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent ability to translate business requirements into technical solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CRM platforms and project management tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with integration technologies such as APIs and ETL processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent written and spoken English, other language skills are beneficial&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication, presentation, and stakeholder management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success in this role will be measured through:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High-quality and customer-focused solution designs and proposals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective support of the sales process resulting in accelerated deal closure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong customer satisfaction with demonstrations, presentations, and proposed solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accuracy and completeness of RFI/RFP responses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successful collaboration across Commercial, Product, Implementation, and Operations teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous contribution to product improvement through market and client insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Increased conversion of qualified opportunities into successful customer engagements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You Should Join Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work with innovative technology solutions in a dynamic commodity trading environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to international clients and complex business challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and entrepreneurial company culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct impact on business growth and customer success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Close interaction with senior stakeholders and industry experts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional development and career growth opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An exciting role at the intersection of technology, consulting, and commercial strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If you are passionate about solving business challenges, working with clients, and delivering innovative solutions that create real value, we&#39;d love to hear from you. Apply today and join our team as a Solutions Consultant&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join Our Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a customer-focused and detail-oriented &lt;strong&gt;Ocean Freight Customer Service Specialist &lt;/strong&gt;to join our growing team. This role is ideal for an experienced logistics or customer service professional who enjoys building strong customer relationships, resolving complex issues, and ensuring the smooth execution of ocean freight bookings and allocation management.&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;As the primary point of contact for our customers, you will play a key role in managing allocations, handling booking-related inquiries, supporting billing processes, and maintaining exceptional service standards across our global freight operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the main point of contact for customer inquiries regarding bookings, allocations, contract terms, and shipment updates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage day-to-day freight allocation requests and coordinate capacity requirements with the procurement team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide timely and accurate information on shipment status, allocation availability, and schedule changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate customer records and case documentation within CRM systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle customer disputes related to freight rates, surcharges, contracts, and service issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and prepare customer invoices, ensuring billing accuracy and commercial compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with carriers, operations, procurement, and finance teams to resolve customer and billing issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor allocation utilization and proactively communicate capacity constraints or opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and close customer cases within agreed service-level targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to customer service reporting and process improvement initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the maintenance and enhancement of customer service procedures and best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate complex customer matters appropriately while ensuring excellent customer experience throughout the resolution process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 3 years of experience in ocean freight, freight forwarding, logistics, or customer service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Business Administration, Logistics, International Trade, or a related field preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of ocean freight operations, shipping documentation, carrier tariffs, and Incoterms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Native-level German and fluent English communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with CRM platforms such as Salesforce, Zendesk, or similar systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read and interpret freight contracts, rate sheets, and customer agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial understanding of ocean freight billing and invoice validation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, especially Outlook, Excel, and Word&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple customer cases and priorities simultaneously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer service or logistics certifications (e.g., FIATA, IATA) are considered an advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Personal Attributes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer-focused with a strong service mentality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving and analytical skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional and composed in challenging customer situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized and able to work effectively under pressure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative team player with excellent communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive, reliable, and solutions-oriented&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptable within a dynamic and fast-paced logistics environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success in this role will be measured through:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High customer satisfaction levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fast response times to customer inquiries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Timely resolution of customer disputes and service issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong case closure performance within SLA targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accurate customer communication and documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High invoice accuracy and low rework rates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective management of freight allocations and booking processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributions to customer service improvements and operational excellence initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You Should Join Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work within a global ocean freight procurement organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to international shipping markets, carrier management, and freight allocation strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative, entrepreneurial, and fast-growing business environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct impact on customer experience and operational performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work closely with procurement, operations, and finance teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional development and career growth opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenging and rewarding role with significant responsibility and customer interaction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modern workplace with an international team culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If you are passionate about customer service, logistics, and building strong customer relationships in the ocean freight industry, we&#39;d love to hear from you. Apply today!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Find Jobs in Switzerland on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Mavericks Wanted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;When was the last time you achieved the impossible? If that thought feels overwhelming, you might want to pause here, but if it sparks excitement...read on&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;In 2015, we pioneered a “moneyball for biotech” approach, pooling projects and promising early-stage research from academia together under one financial umbrella to reduce risk and unleash innovation. This model allows science and small teams of experts to lead the way. We build bridges to groundbreaking advancements in rare&amp;nbsp;disease, and&amp;nbsp;develop life-changing medicines for patients with unmet needs as fast as humanly possible. &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Together we define white space, push boundaries, and empower people to solve problems. If you&#39;re someone who defies convention, join us and work alongside some of the most respected minds in the industry. Together, we&#39;ll&amp;nbsp;ask&amp;nbsp;&quot;why not?&quot; and help reengineer the future of biopharma. At BridgeBio, we value curiosity and experimentation—including the ethical &amp;amp; thoughtful use of AI to improve clarity, speed, and quality of work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;About BridgeBio Pharma, Inc.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BridgeBio is a biopharmaceutical company dedicated to discovering, developing, and delivering transformative medicines for patients living with genetic diseases and genetically defined cancers. Since our founding in 2015, we have built a diverse portfolio of more than 20 drug development programs, ranging from early discovery to late-stage clinical trials, across multiple therapeutic areas including precision oncology, cardiology, endocrinology, neurology, and renal disease. We have already achieved regulatory approval for three therapies and continue to advance promising science from academia into meaningful treatments for patients worldwide.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Who We Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BridgeBio is a global biotechnology company with our Global Headquarters located in San Francisco, USA, and our International HQ located in Zug, Switzerland. Since establishing our European presence in 2021, we’ve been building empowered, high-performing teams across countries — with experienced colleagues who move quickly, take ownership, and are fueling the company’s international growth.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At BridgeBio, you’ll find an energetic and collaborative culture where pragmatism meets bold decision-making. We embrace uncertainty with confidence, guided by our commitment to making a meaningful impact for patients. Our people are trusted and empowered, united by urgency, purpose, and the drive to advance science for patients around the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To learn more about our story and company culture, visit us at &lt;a href=&quot;https://bridgebio.com&quot;&gt;https://bridgebio.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report to the VP, Head of Market Access, International and work closely with international Market Access, regional brand team, and heads or markets access in BridgeBio clusters as well as with field-based colleagues across multiple geographies, to drive strategic initiatives that support BridgeBio’s mission of delivering transformative medicines to patients globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your primary purpose will be to secure timely, sustainable patient access to the company’s products by shaping the value narrative, and leading pricing and reimbursement strategies and execution across multiple international markets. This includes oversight of related dossiers, negotiations, and cost coverage approaches. In this role you ensure alignment of Market Access ambitions with clinical value and global pricing interdependencies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will also be a core member of the International Market Access team, contributing to global decision-making and ensuring alignment across regions while representing diverse market perspectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires strong collaboration with cross-functional colleagues and external stakeholders across multiple countries to ensure high-quality execution and impact. The ideal candidate combines deep expertise in Market Access processes across several international markets and experience introducing innovative therapies in a global biotech environment. You are eager to make a meaningful contribution in pre-launch and launch phases, particularly within rare diseases and orphan conditions, and bring strong communication skills, adaptability, and the ability to thrive in a fast-paced, hands-on environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the payer perspective within cross-functional, cross-regional commercialization teams thereby optimizing pricing and market access of the asset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Closely collaborate with HEOR and clusters&#39; leadership teams, Marketing and Clinical Development counterparts to ensure value and access optimization for the asset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead early payer engagement with key HTA/payer bodies (e.g. NICE UK, G-BA Germany) to inform evidence generation strategy, value proposition and reimbursement dossiers development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interact with internal and external experts in pricing, health economics, patient advocacy, health technology assessment authorities, government policy makers and payers as required to execute Pricing &amp;amp; Reimbursement objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide hands-on support and train local access teams on negotiation strategy and ensure HTA and reimbursement submissions are aligned to the Global and International strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Where You’ll Work&amp;nbsp; &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an office role based and requires in-office collaboration 2-3x per week in our Zug Office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Who You Are&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience leading HTA submissions and pricing negotiations across multiple international markets, ideally including Europe and other global regions, particularly in rare diseases and orphan conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of international healthcare systems, pricing and reimbursement frameworks, and regulatory environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience generating and leveraging data for HTA submissions and pricing negotiations, with a strong external network of agencies and stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable presenting at senior levels and engaging with external thought leaders globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience managing complex, cross-functional and multicultural teams (including external partners).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of product commercialization processes with a hands-on, solution-oriented mindset for building scalable processes and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Rewarding Those Who Make the Mission Possible&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have high expectations for our team members. We make sure those working hard for patients are rewarded and cared for in return.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market leading compensation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid work model - we value your flexibility in how you work, but encourage time in the office to strengthen our culture, collaboration, and sense of community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We provide career development through regular feedback, continuous education and professional development programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We celebrate strong performance with financial rewards, peer-to-peer recognition, and growth opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a global company, our comprehensive benefits may vary based on location.&amp;nbsp; &lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We have high expectations for our team members. We make sure those working hard for patients are rewarded and cared for in return.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;For BridgeBio Full-Time U.S Based Roles:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
