&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Supervisor: &lt;/strong&gt;Prof. Dr. Alexander Tormasov&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Constructor Knowledge Labs (CKL), in collaboration with Constructor Technology, invites applications for a PhD position in machine learning for software engineering and formal methods, on the Constructor Fabric project.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Constructor Fabric turns a company&#39;s informal knowledge into production software through a pipeline of composable capability units called &lt;em&gt;gears&lt;/em&gt;: requirements → architecture → product fit → framework (G1) → application → runtime. We are building a &lt;strong&gt;World Model&lt;/strong&gt; over that pipeline — a model that does not just generate code, but predicts the &lt;em&gt;consequences&lt;/em&gt; of an architectural decision: total cost of ownership, unintended side effects, latency and failure behaviour, and whether a proposed composition is even admissible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;The central object is not a digital twin of the application but its &lt;strong&gt;formal architectural skeleton&lt;/strong&gt;: gear contracts (GearSpec), a typed attributed hypergraph of the application (AppGraph), a composition algebra that defines which assemblies are legal, and several semantic projections (types, protocols, resources, security) over which properties are proved, refuted by counterexample, or reported as an explainable &lt;strong&gt;gap&lt;/strong&gt;. All of it is written in a &lt;strong&gt;domain-specific language&lt;/strong&gt; whose syntax trees and graphs we keep in a projectional editor (JetBrains MPS) — so the DSL is not a convenience layer, it is the thing that defines the model&#39;s state space and the boundary of what the model is allowed to propose.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will work on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Depending on your background, one or two of:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Formal skeleton and composition — GearSpec as a contract $(Requires, Provides, State, Effects, Assumptions, Guarantees, Parameters)$; AppGraph as a typed attributed hypergraph; an algebra of assembly (sequential, parallel, feedback, refinement); semantic projections and system-level invariants over trajectories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architecture synthesis as an inverse problem — given a specification, load and constraints, find the composition of gears that realises it. Constraint solving and MCTS as the baseline; a learned transition/value model for ranking and pruning; LLM proposals treated strictly as candidate hypotheses that a DSL parser, type checker and property checks must then admit or reject.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DSL design and language engineering — the gear DSL and its glue layer decide which AppGraphs are expressible at all, and therefore where the search space ends. This thread covers the abstract syntax and static semantics of that DSL; the requirement that an architectural decision be unbypassable by construction (you must not be able to wire authentication around the Auth Resolver); what happens to the language when gear contracts change or a 201st gear is added; projectional representation of graphs with cycles; and the open hypothesis that a specialised G1-DSL is generated together with every G1.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Local transition models and pipeline surrogates — fast approximate predictors for single pipeline steps (spec change → code quality, architecture → product fit, app → runtime outcome), with calibrated uncertainty, validated against real telemetry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data — reconstructing (specification → architecture) pairs from open repositories at scale, plus synthetic project generation from a fixed gear set and DSL grammar to cover rare transitions, gaps and counterexamples.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MSc (or equivalent) in computer science, mathematics, or a mathematical natural science.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coursework in compilers, programming-language theory, language design or model-driven engineering is a strong positive signal, half of this project is deciding what a formal architecture description is allowed to say.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evidence that you finish things: a maintained open-source repository, a peer-reviewed publication, or a strong competition result.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent technical English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Most importantly: the habit of stating an assumption explicitly and designing an experiment that could falsify it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required mathematical background&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Core skills:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Probability and statistics. Estimation, Bayesian inference, uncertainty quantification and calibration (proper scoring rules, reliability diagrams, ECE), experiment design and significance testing. A prediction we cannot calibrate is not usable here.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Linear algebra and multivariate calculus at the level needed to derive, not just call, a training objective: matrix calculus, gradients, stochastic optimisation, conditioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discrete mathematics and graph theory. Typed and attributed graphs and hypergraphs, subgraph matching and isomorphism, graph rewriting, reachability, basic complexity classes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mathematical logic and formal methods. First-order logic, type systems, SAT/SMT, temporal logic (LTL/CTL) and model checking, pre/post-conditions, invariants, refinement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sequential decision making. MDP/POMDP, dynamic programming, model-based RL, latent state-space (world) models, Monte-Carlo Tree Search.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Strong command of at least one, working knowledge of a second:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Formal languages, semantics and language engineering — grammars (context-free, attribute and graph grammars), derivation and reachability, parsing; abstract versus concrete syntax; operational and denotational semantics; metamodelling, model-driven engineering, model-to-model transformation, and projectional (structural) editing of the kind JetBrains MPS implements. We are asking for the education, not the tool: you should know why a projectional editor exists, what a metamodel buys you over a text grammar, and how a language evolves without breaking its existing models. Hands-on MPS experience is explicitly not required — we will teach it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Category theory for compositional systems — monoidal and traced monoidal categories, functors as semantic projections, string diagrams, operads. This is the language of our assembly algebra.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Causal inference — structural causal models, do-calculus, counterfactuals, identifiability. Required for the &quot;what happens if we replace this technology / move on-premises&quot; class of questions, which similarity search alone cannot answer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Queueing theory and applied stochastic processes — M/M/1 and networks of queues, heavy tails, retries, timeouts, partial failure and reliability models. This is the resource and stochastic projection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Combinatorial optimisation, constraint programming and program synthesis theory — CEGIS, version-space algebras, symmetry breaking, search heuristics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Representation learning theory — VAEs and latent dynamics, GNN expressiveness (Weisfeiler-Leman hierarchy), permutation equivariance, embedding migration under a changing vocabulary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required hands-on programming skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an engineering-heavy PhD. We expect code that another person can clone, run and reproduce — not notebooks that worked once.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Must have:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python (professional level). Type hints, packaging, `pytest`, profiling, `asyncio`, memory-aware data structures. You write unbuffered, logged, restartable long-running jobs by default.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Training loops written from scratch, custom datasets and collation, mixed precision, multi-GPU; experiment tracking (W&amp;amp;B or MLflow), configuration management (Hydra), strict seed and artefact reproducibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Graph machine learning. PyTorch Geometric or DGL — message passing, heterogeneous and typed graphs, graph transformers, handling graphs whose node vocabulary changes between versions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solvers and verification tooling driven from Python. Z3 or cvc5 hands-on; demonstrated exposure to at least one model checker (TLA+/TLC, SPIN, NuSMV, Alloy) or proof assistant (Lean, Coq, Isabelle).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Code as data. AST manipulation, `tree-sitter`, static analysis, dependency and interface graph extraction, large-scale repository mining.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parallel data pipelines. `multiprocessing`, Ray or Dask; checkpointing, heartbeats, cost estimation before launching a run that touches millions of files.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;LLM engineering. API orchestration, structured and grammar-constrained decoding, evaluation harnesses, token/cost accounting — with the discipline to treat model output as a hypothesis subject to formal checks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Linux, git, code review, shell.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Desirable:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Language tooling you have actually used: ANTLR, Xtext, Lark, or a parser, type checker or interpreter you wrote yourself. Our internal representation of gear syntax trees and graphs lives in JetBrains MPS — again, we do not ask for MPS experience, only that you are comfortable reading and extending a metamodel; Java/Kotlin literacy helps once you get there.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JAX, or compiler / SAT-SMT internals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Infrastructure literacy — Docker, Kubernetes, Terraform, OpenTelemetry/Prometheus — since the resource projection is calibrated against real deployment telemetry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;One systems language (Rust, Go or C++) for performance-critical search.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience with production software architecture, or with a brownfield system you had to change without breaking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Funding&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The appointment provides full financial coverage through a dedicated fellowship, comprising:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly stipend of €1,650&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly research-cost allowance of €100 (Forschungskostenpauschale)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health-insurance subsidy of €100 per month&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;Bremen, Germany&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duration: &lt;/strong&gt;3 years, full time&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Start date: &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;November 2026&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application package must include&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CV, including publications, code, or research projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cover letter (1–2 pages) explaining your motivation, research interests, and fit with the project.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A link to code you have written.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A one-page research statement picking one open research question from the project and sketching how you would approach it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s and Bachelor’s degree certificate and transcripts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contact information for 2–3 academic referees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Applications are reviewed on a rolling basis. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to interviews.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;heading 2&quot;&gt;About us&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134245418&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:280,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:100}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://constructorlabs.org/&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;Constructor Labs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; is the research arm of Constructor Knowledge, based at Campus Ring 1 in Bremen, Germany. Our work is organized around three units: Knowledge Labs, Cyber Labs and Science Labs. We apply computing, software and robotics research to make scientists, teachers and students more effective, working with institutional partners that include CERN, NUS, Carnegie Mellon and Fraunhofer.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://constructor.tech/products/learning/practice&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;Constructor Practice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; is the hands-on practice platform within the Constructor Technology learning suite, alongside Learn, Assess, Proctor, Schedule and Groups. It spans an unusually broad portfolio: curriculum-aligned virtual science labs; the evidence-based intervention products Calcularis (numeracy and dyscalculia), Grafari/Orthograph (literacy and dyslexia); and browser-based Software &amp;amp; IT and Coding labs for technical training. Shared capabilities include cloud-based hands-on environments with no installation, automated assessment and grading, group assignments and instructor assistance, LMS integration, and learner analytics and dashboards.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The product is in production across three distinct markets. Higher education and research, schools and public education authorities, and corporate and vocational training. The platform operates under GDPR, FERPA, COPPA and SOPIPA commitments.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;About the Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;You will own Constructor Practice content portfolio of products (currently includes Practice: Science Labs and Practice: Schools Math and Literacy with future extension to other disciplines) end to end: strategy, roadmap, commercial performance and delivery. This is a lead product management position with full accountability for the product line rather than for a single feature area or squad.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The scope is wider than a conventional PM role. You will sit in front of clients during presales, shape the go-to-market with sales and marketing, define the roadmap across a portfolio serving three different buyer types, and work with product owners and engineering to bring releases in on time and on budget. Where the product line needs something that has no owner, it is yours.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Practice has an established customer base and a portfolio that has grown through acquisition and expansion into markets with little in common: a Swiss canton buying dyscalculia intervention for primary schools has almost nothing in common with Acronis training its partner ecosystem. Bringing coherence to that portfolio, deciding what to invest in, what to standardize and what to retire, is the central problem of this role.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;heading 2&quot;&gt;Reporting and scope&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134245418&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:280,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:100}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;•&quot; data-font=&quot;&quot; data-listid=&quot;2&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;•&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;1&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Reports to:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Head of SI and Edu, Constructor Labs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;•&quot; data-font=&quot;&quot; data-listid=&quot;2&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;•&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;2&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Level:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Lead Product Manager. You will lead the product team including product owners, engineers and subject matter experts, with a view to building a larger product team as the line grows.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;•&quot; data-font=&quot;&quot; data-listid=&quot;2&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;•&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;3&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Product surface:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; all Constructor Practice content products, namely Science Labs, Calcularis, Grafari/Orthograph, Software &amp;amp; IT and Coding, in cooperation with the shared platform layer covering assessment, analytics, LMS integration and deployment.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;•&quot; data-font=&quot;&quot; data-listid=&quot;2&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;•&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;4&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Markets:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; higher education and research institutions, schools and public education authorities, and corporate and vocational training providers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;•&quot; data-font=&quot;&quot; data-listid=&quot;2&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;•&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;5&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Interfaces:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; engineering and product owners, presales and sales, marketing, customer success and support, Constructor Tech engineering and product teams, Nexademy content team, Constructor Labs research, and Constructor Labs Solutions as an integration channel.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The role is both outward and inward facing. You are expected to be in client conversations and in sprint reviews in the same week, and to carry what you learn in one into the other.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duties &amp;amp; Responsibilities&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Product strategy.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Set the direction for Practice across its three markets: where to invest, where to standardize on shared platform capability, and where a module should be sustained rather than developed. Maintain a defensible view of the competitive position against virtual lab providers, intervention software and hands-on technical training platforms.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Roadmap and prioritization.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Own a published roadmap with a clear rationale for sequencing, balancing client commitments, platform debt, regulatory requirements and new capability. Say no in a way that holds up, and keep the roadmap current as commitments change.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Discovery and requirements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Work directly with teachers, learning designers, lab administrators, IT staff and corporate training leads to establish what the product needs to do. Translate that into specifications, acceptance criteria and measurable outcomes rather than feature lists.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Delivery with engineering.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Work with product owners and development teams through planning, sprint reviews and release. Hold scope, schedule and budget together, escalate early when one of the three has to give, and make the trade-off explicit rather than absorbing it quietly.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Presales support.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Act as the product authority in qualified opportunities: demonstrations, solution design, technical objection handling, RFP and tender responses, security and compliance questionnaires. Judge which client-specific requests are viable and which are not.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Go-to-market.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Own positioning, messaging and the launch plan for each release and module, working with marketing and sales enablement. Produce the materials that let the sales team sell Practice without you in the room.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Client relationships.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Run a regular cadence with reference and strategic accounts, gather structured feedback, manage expectations on committed features and turn successful deployments into case studies and references.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Pricing and commercials.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Own the pricing and packaging model across modules and market segments, with input on licensing, bundling within the Constructor learning suite, and the commercial terms of custom work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Compliance and trust.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Keep the product aligned with GDPR, FERPA, COPPA and SOPIPA obligations and with accessibility requirements, working with legal and security. Child-facing products in public education carry a higher bar, and meeting it is part of the roadmap.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Performance measurement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Instrument the product, track adoption, engagement and learning outcomes, and use the evidence to decide what to build next and what to stop.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Product ownership at scale.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Five or more years in product management, including at least three owning a B2B SaaS product line with revenue accountability rather than a single feature area.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Education or adjacent domain.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Experience with EdTech, assessment, e-learning, corporate L&amp;amp;D tooling or another domain where the buyer, the administrator and the end user are three different people with different measures of success.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Delivery discipline.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; A track record of shipping on committed dates and budgets with agile teams, working through product owners and engineering leads, and managing the scope conversations that make that possible.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Commercial fluency.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Comfort in front of clients and in presales, with the ability to run a demonstration, defend a roadmap position and contribute to pricing and packaging decisions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Technical credibility.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Enough depth in cloud platforms, LMS integration standards such as LTI and SCORM, APIs and analytics to hold your own with engineering and with a client&#39;s IT team, without needing to write the code yourself.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Evidence-based decisions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Fluency with product analytics and experimentation, and the judgement to distinguish a signal worth acting on from a loud customer.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Portfolio judgement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Experience managing several products or modules at once, and a willingness to make and defend investment and retirement decisions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Languages.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Business-fluent English. German is a bonus, given the Swiss, German and Austrian school and public-sector customer base.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Communication.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Written and verbal clarity with audiences ranging from a primary school teacher to a university CIO to a development team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;heading 2&quot;&gt;Nice to have&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134245418&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:280,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:100}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;•&quot; data-font=&quot;&quot; data-listid=&quot;4&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;•&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;16&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Experience with virtual labs, simulation environments or browser-based development and IT training environments.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;•&quot; data-font=&quot;&quot; data-listid=&quot;4&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;•&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;17&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Background in special educational needs, learning intervention or evidence-based pedagogy, particularly dyscalculia or dyslexia support.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;•&quot; data-font=&quot;&quot; data-listid=&quot;4&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;•&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;18&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Familiarity with public-sector education procurement in DACH, including cantonal and Länder-level buying.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;•&quot; data-font=&quot;&quot; data-listid=&quot;4&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;•&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;19&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Experience with student data privacy regimes (GDPR in an education context, FERPA, COPPA, SOPIPA) and WCAG accessibility conformance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;•&quot; data-font=&quot;&quot; data-listid=&quot;4&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;•&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;20&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Prior work in a group structure where a product is sold both directly and through an integration or services channel.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;•&quot; data-font=&quot;&quot; data-listid=&quot;4&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;•&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;21&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;A background in teaching, instructional design or learning science.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;heading 2&quot;&gt;What we offer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134245418&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:280,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:100}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;•&quot; data-font=&quot;&quot; data-listid=&quot;5&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;•&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;22&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;A product line with an established base&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;, in production with universities, public education authorities and corporate academies across Europe and beyond.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;•&quot; data-font=&quot;&quot; data-listid=&quot;5&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;•&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;23&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Genuine end-to-end ownership&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;, from strategy and pricing through to release, without the role being split across a commercial owner and a delivery owner.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;•&quot; data-font=&quot;&quot; data-listid=&quot;5&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;•&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;24&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Access to our researchers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;, including principal investigators and education methodologists from Constructor Labs, and the ability to route applied research questions into the Labs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;•&quot; data-font=&quot;&quot; data-listid=&quot;5&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;•&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;25&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Salary and annual bonus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; tied to the product line&#39;s commercial and delivery targets. The band is competitive for a lead product role in DACH or the UK and depends on location and experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;•&quot; data-font=&quot;&quot; data-listid=&quot;5&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;•&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;26&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;A distribution channel beyond direct sales&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;, through Constructor Labs Solutions and the partner network.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Project&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Constructor Fabric turns a company&#39;s informal knowledge into production software through a pipeline of composable capability units called &lt;em&gt;gears&lt;/em&gt;: requirements → architecture → product fit → framework (G1) → application → runtime. We are building a &lt;strong&gt;World Model&lt;/strong&gt; over that pipeline — a model that does not just generate code, but predicts the &lt;em&gt;consequences&lt;/em&gt; of an architectural decision: total cost of ownership, unintended side effects, latency and failure behaviour, and whether a proposed composition is even admissible.&lt;br&gt;The central object is not a digital twin of the application but its &lt;strong&gt;formal architectural skeleton&lt;/strong&gt;: gear contracts (GearSpec), a typed attributed hypergraph of the application (AppGraph), a composition algebra that defines which assemblies are legal, and several semantic projections (types, protocols, resources, security) over which properties are proved, refuted by counterexample, or reported as an explainable &lt;strong&gt;gap&lt;/strong&gt;. All of it is written in a &lt;strong&gt;domain-specific language&lt;/strong&gt; whose syntax trees and graphs we keep in a projectional editor (JetBrains MPS) — so the DSL is not a convenience layer, it is the thing that defines the model&#39;s state space and the boundary of what the model is allowed to propose.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Internship Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Research Intern (Machine Learning for Software Engineering), you will support the data and modelling work behind the World Model — mining code, building datasets, and running baseline experiments. We are looking for students who are keen to collaborate with industrial companies working with AI, open to out-of-the-box topics, and interested in a long-term collaboration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mine open-source repositories and extract architecture, dependency, and interface graphs from code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build and clean (specification → architecture) datasets, including synthetic project generation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and evaluate baseline models (heuristic search, graph ML, or LLM generation) for single pipeline steps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Benchmark models against shared datasets and metrics to compare approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build evaluation harnesses and track experiments reproducibly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with documentation and, where relevant, publication activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently enrolled in a BSc/MSc in Computer Science, Data Science, Mathematics, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Python and ML frameworks (PyTorch, scikit-learn).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in machine learning for code, software engineering, or formal methods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good English and teamwork skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Predictive models/time-series/etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;LLM tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with graph machine learning (PyTorch Geometric or DGL).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in formal methods, program or static analysis, or working with code structure (e.g. AST manipulation, tree-sitter, or repository mining).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application Details&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please submit:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CV&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Short motivation letter (max. 1 page) explaining your interest and relevant skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Transcript of records (GPA obligatory)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;Remote within Europe, with regular presence in Bremen&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct Reports:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;None initially&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working Model: &lt;/strong&gt;Remote / hybrid. Regular time on-site in Bremen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Mission&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the product direction for Constructor&#39;s quantum software line and act as the bridge between a research group and a technology platform. This is a hands-on role in a small technical team, not portfolio management. The Head of Product decides what gets built, keeps research and engineering pointed at something shippable, and owns the relationship with the customers and partners who use it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar 1 Product Direction&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the roadmap for the quantum software line and the decisions behind it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define which capabilities go into the Constructor technology platform and in what order.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate research capability into product that someone outside the group will pay for or use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kill work that is not going anywhere, and say so clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Success Metrics and KPIs: roadmap delivered, features adopted, decisions made and held.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar 2 Research and Engineering Interface&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sit between physicists and engineers and keep both productive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run planning and prioritisation for a small, senior, opinionated team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold the technical depth to challenge both sides rather than relay between them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Accountability: research output converted into shipped product.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar 3 External Engagement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own customer, partner and vendor relationships directly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Constructor Tech and Constructor University on joint offerings and teaching applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the group externally at conferences and with partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Success Metrics and KPIs: partner engagements initiated and sustained, external visibility of the group.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical background in physics, engineering or computer science, with enough depth to hold your own with research scientists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Taken scientific or deep-tech software from research prototype to product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run customer and partner engagements personally, not through a sales team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Worked somewhere small enough that the product person also does the work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong facilitation. You will be the person keeping a room of physicists on track.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable being the only product person present.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to say no and explain why.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication with technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education &amp;amp; Languages&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in a technical discipline; postgraduate qualification an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What This Role Is (and Is Not)&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role IS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on, senior, and accountable for what the group ships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A role with real decision authority over direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Externally facing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is NOT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A programme or portfolio management role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A role with a product team reporting into it from day one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A commercial role without technical substance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Remote within Europe, with regular presence in Bremen&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct Reports:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working Model: &lt;/strong&gt;Remote / hybrid. Regular time on-site in Bremen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Mission&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own build, deployment and infrastructure for scientific software that runs in awkward places — customer premises, restricted laboratory networks, air-gapped sites, and our own cloud. The role combines conventional cloud platform engineering with the harder problem of shipping updatable software into environments we do not control.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar 1 Deployment and Delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own build, CI/CD and release for the platform across cloud and on-premise targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain installers and update paths that work in restricted and offline environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage database migration and rollback paths for customer installations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Success Metrics and KPIs: release frequency, failed deployments, time to patch a customer site.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar 2 Infrastructure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the Kubernetes and GitOps side of the platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own secrets management, access control and infrastructure-as-code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement monitoring and log aggregation across internal and customer environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate with Constructor&#39;s platform, identity and deployment tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Success Metrics and KPIs: uptime, mean time to detect, infrastructure reproducible from code.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar 3 Security and Governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Introduce static analysis and dependency and licence scanning into the pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own backup, recovery and continuity for the platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support audit and compliance requirements from funded research and customer contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Accountability: no single undocumented dependency on one person, including yourself.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong AWS or equivalent, Kubernetes, and configuration management such as Ansible, at production scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real experience of on-premise and offline deployment, not only cloud.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CI/CD pipeline ownership end to end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Autonomous and proactive. You have carried infrastructure alone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to hand knowledge over rather than hold it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interested in the product and the science, not only the pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communicator in English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education &amp;amp; Languages&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in computer science or engineering, or equivalent practical track record.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What This Role Is (and Is Not)&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role IS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full ownership of infrastructure for a technically unusual product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A role where you finally get a team around you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to a broad modern stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is NOT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A pure cloud or pure on-premise role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A ticket-driven operations role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A role without contact with the product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CSQ427R35&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Forward Deployed Engineer (FDE) you will work with customers to build and productionize solutions to their data &amp;amp; AI challenges using the Databricks platform. You will own the architecture, lead design decisions, and implement end-to-end systems spanning data engineering, AI, and application development. We work cross-functionally to shape long-term strategic priorities and initiatives alongside engineering, product, and developer relations. FDEs deliver with customer empathy, integrating with client systems, training, and other technical needs to help customers get most value out of their data.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on, customer-facing role for builders who thrive at the intersection of technology and business impact. The ideal candidate combines engineering expertise with adaptability, curiosity, and a passion for working with customers and teammates to solve complex problems that drive measurable outcomes. FDEs are billable and know how to complete projects according to specification with exceptional customer empathy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The impact you will have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production Solution Delivery: Lead impactful customer technical projects by delivering production-grade systems, designing and building reference architectures, custom applications and data ingestion and ML/AI model integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Transformational Impact: Guide strategic customers as they implement transformational big data projects including end-to-end design, build and deployment of industry-leading big data and AI applications. Work with engagement managers to scope technical delivery work with input from the customer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empower Customers: Guide customers on architecture and design; bootstrap or implement customer projects which leads to a customers&#39; successful understanding, evaluation and adoption of Databricks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Architecture: Lead architecture and design decisions, ensuring solutions are secure, scalable, and aligned with both customer needs and Databricks best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the Databricks technical team, Project Manager, Architect and Customer team to ensure the technical components of the engagement are delivered to meet customer&#39;s needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Engineering and Databricks Customer Support to provide product and implementation feedback and to guide rapid resolution for engagement specific product and support issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer Immersion: Embed with customer teams, engaging with stakeholders from technical ICs to executives to deeply understand challenges and deliver impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reusable Assets &amp;amp; Scale: Contribute accelerators, frameworks, and best practices that scale impact across accounts and influence the Databricks product roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years experience in data engineering, data platforms &amp;amp; analytics, or software engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable writing code in either Python, Scala, JavaScript/TypeScript, and modern frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of two or more common Cloud ecosystems (AWS, Azure, GCP) with expertise in at least one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with distributed computing with Apache Spark™ and knowledge of Spark runtime internals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with CI/CD for production deployments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of MLOps, ML/AI models and AI APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and deployment of performant production end-to-end data architectures and applications that combine data pipelines, ML/AI models, and user-facing interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with technical project delivery - managing scope, timelines and measurable outcomes, translating complex concepts into actionable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Documentation and white-boarding skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with enterprise clients and managing conflicts across a broad stakeholder range&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build skills in technical areas, and demonstrate curiosity, adaptability, and eagerness to explore new technologies which support the deployment and integration of Databricks-based solutions to complete customer projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel to customers 20% of the time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Databricks Certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Databricks is the Data and AI company. More than 20,000 organizations worldwide — including adidas, AT&amp;amp;T, Bayer, Block, Mastercard, Rivian, Unilever, and 70% of the Fortune 500 — rely on the Databricks Data + AI Platform to build and scale data and AI apps, analytics and agents. Headquartered in San Francisco with 30+ offices around the globe, Databricks offers a unified platform that includes Genie, Lakebase, Agent Bricks, Lakeflow, Lakehouse, and Unity Catalog. To learn more, follow Databricks on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/databricks&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/databricks&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/@Databricks&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/databricksinc/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;At Databricks, we strive to provide comprehensive benefits and perks that meet the needs of all of our employees. For specific details on the benefits offered in your region click &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/154un3e8Xav4BceOSlcYFZRGEuQI54xMxVydRwQn54eQ/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive culture where everyone can excel. We take great care to ensure that our hiring practices are inclusive and meet equal employment opportunity standards. Individuals looking for employment at Databricks are considered without regard to age, color, disability, ethnicity, family or marital status, gender identity or expression, language, national origin, physical and mental ability, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, veteran status, and other protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If access to export-controlled technology or source code is required for performance of job duties, it is within Employer&#39;s discretion whether to apply for a U.S. government license for such positions, and Employer may decline to proceed with an applicant on this basis alone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SLSQ427R368&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While candidates in the listed locations are encouraged for this role, we are open to remote candidates in other locations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This senior leadership role&lt;/strong&gt; will lead Partner Sales for the&amp;nbsp; Central EMEA region (Germany. CH, Austria eastern Europe), focused on consulting and Systems Integrator (C&amp;amp;SI) partners, as a member of the Regional Leadership Team. The regional leader will build the regional ecosystem strategy and plan aligned with regional and functional priorities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your direct reports will include Partner Sales managers/directors in the region. You will report to the Vice President, EMEA Alliances.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Director, Partner Sales, you own the partner go-to-market strategy for the assigned region — driving co-sell motions in our top accounts, working with priority partners for co-sell and co-deliver, building durable pipelines, and holding partners accountable to execution that converts to partner-sourced and partner-influenced consumption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly visible, strategic role: you drive the partner-first motion across Sales, Field Engineering, Marketing, and work with the extended team of Partner Solution Architects, Partner Marketing, Partner Management and Partner Enablement. You carry Databricks&#39; regional partner narrative to senior partner executives in our partner ecosystem. You will own and grow executive relationships and commitment with strategic partners across the region — including global and regional systems integrators (e.g. Accenture, Deloitte, Capgemini) and specialist data and AI partners — and you bring deep industry knowledge and an operator&#39;s mindset powered by modern AI tooling.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2006&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;The impact you will have: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership &amp;amp; Team Development&lt;/strong&gt; — Lead the regional Alliances/C&amp;amp;SI function, building and developing a high-performing cross-functional team while representing the partner organisation in regional leadership forums.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Planning &amp;amp; Ecosystem Leadership&lt;/strong&gt; — Own the multi-year regional partner territory plan — forming a compelling 3-year vision with partner segmentation, coverage model, and operational rhythm aligned to regional and functional priorities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Relationships &amp;amp; Narrative&lt;/strong&gt; — Own executive-level partner relationships, building joint business plans and executive-ready narratives that represent Databricks credibly to senior partner and customer leadership.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Account-Level Co-Sell &amp;amp; Big Bet Workshops&lt;/strong&gt; — Drive joint account planning workshops in Top/must-win accounts with priority partners as the primary co-sell and pipeline creation mechanism; coach AEs and scale the partner motion through the field.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pipeline &amp;amp; Revenue Engine&lt;/strong&gt; — Architect the regional partner GTM strategy and convert it into a tangible, partner-sourced and partner-influenced pipeline and consumption. Drive partner-led demand generation at scale — industry events, co-funded campaigns, partner pitch days, and regional kickoff sponsorships.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product-Specific Partner GTM&lt;/strong&gt; — Own product-specific partner campaigns (Migration &amp;amp; Modernisation, Genie, Lakebase, AgentBricks) aligned to platform priorities; proactively build partner capability on new products to maintain delivery coverage as the product mix evolves.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner Execution &amp;amp; Accountability&lt;/strong&gt; — Hold strategic SI partners and tiered programme partners (Gold/Silver) to joint commitments on both delivery capability and business development; run a disciplined operating cadence of pipeline reviews, forecast, and KPI inspection anchored to Salesforce; report impact, not activity.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner Delivery Quality&lt;/strong&gt; — Own partner delivery quality governance — resolve escalations, ensure partners&#39; staff to SoW, and work with FDE/Field Engineering on delivery models that protect customer outcomes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Orchestration &amp;amp; Field Adoption&lt;/strong&gt; — Set direction across Sales, Field Engineering, Marketing, and Partner Solution Architecture; embed partner strategy into territory reviews and drive internal field adoption so AEs actively engage partners in their accounts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solution Development &amp;amp; Delivery Readiness&lt;/strong&gt; — Co-create differentiated, industry-specific joint solutions and repeatable GTM campaigns while supporting SI partner practice development through enablement, asset development, and delivery excellence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-Driven Operations&lt;/strong&gt; — Use AI tools as the primary operating system for pipeline inspection, partner intelligence, exec meeting prep, and partner-facing demos; drive AI fluency across the partner ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2367&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;What we look for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership Experience&lt;/strong&gt; — Proven people leader who has built and scaled teams of partner sales directors/managers, operating as a member of a partner or regional leadership team in a leading software company.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner/Alliance Sales Experience&lt;/strong&gt; — Extensive experience in partner/alliance sales, channel, or GTM at an enterprise software, cloud, or data company with a proven track record of building partner-sourced pipeline and driving measurable revenue impact.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SI &amp;amp; Executive Engagement&lt;/strong&gt; — Specific experience working with Global and Regional Systems Integrators at an executive level to lead industry GTM activation, CXO engagement, and transformational outcomes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Account-Level Co-Sell Execution&lt;/strong&gt; — Demonstrated ability to drive joint account planning workshops with SI partners in enterprise accounts, translating partner capability into sourced pipeline and closed consumption.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Leadership &amp;amp; Field Influence&lt;/strong&gt; — Track record leading across Sales, Field/Technical, Marketing, Cloud partners (AWS, Azure, GCP), and SI/ISV partners in a matrixed environment; proven ability to embed partner strategy into field operating rhythms and influence AEs without direct authority.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Presence&lt;/strong&gt; — Shapes a compelling business narrative and aligns senior internal, partner, and customer stakeholders; represents Databricks credibly at the CXO level.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Rigour&lt;/strong&gt; — Clean pipeline hygiene, KPI discipline, and data-driven inspection; comfort defining and running OKRs that drive predictability in partner-sourced pipeline.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner Delivery Governance&lt;/strong&gt; — Experience managing partner delivery quality — resolving escalations, holding partners to SoW commitments, and working with professional services on co-delivery models.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Industry &amp;amp; Domain Expertise&lt;/strong&gt; — Deep knowledge of SI business models, industry workflows, and regional buying patterns; understands how data and AI create value and translates use cases into joint partner solutions.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Fluency &amp;amp; Travel&lt;/strong&gt; — Fluency with modern AI productivity tools, including AI-powered analytics for pipeline and partner intelligence; ability to travel 25–40% for partner business reviews, account-planning workshops, and executive engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Databricks is the Data and AI company. More than 20,000 organizations worldwide — including adidas, AT&amp;amp;T, Bayer, Block, Mastercard, Rivian, Unilever, and 70% of the Fortune 500 — rely on the Databricks Data + AI Platform to build and scale data and AI apps, analytics and agents. Headquartered in San Francisco with 30+ offices around the globe, Databricks offers a unified platform that includes Genie, Lakebase, Agent Bricks, Lakeflow, Lakehouse, and Unity Catalog. To learn more, follow Databricks on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/databricks&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/databricks&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/@Databricks&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/databricksinc/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;At Databricks, we strive to provide comprehensive benefits and perks that meet the needs of all of our employees. For specific details on the benefits offered in your region click &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/154un3e8Xav4BceOSlcYFZRGEuQI54xMxVydRwQn54eQ/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive culture where everyone can excel. We take great care to ensure that our hiring practices are inclusive and meet equal employment opportunity standards. Individuals looking for employment at Databricks are considered without regard to age, color, disability, ethnicity, family or marital status, gender identity or expression, language, national origin, physical and mental ability, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, veteran status, and other protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If access to export-controlled technology or source code is required for performance of job duties, it is within Employer&#39;s discretion whether to apply for a U.S. government license for such positions, and Employer may decline to proceed with an applicant on this basis alone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;sc-gEkIjz cjtSrT MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 sc-hoLEA&quot;&gt;Raisin is the world’s leading platform for savings and investment products. Founded in 2012, the&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;FinTech&lt;/strong&gt; connects consumers with banks in the EU, the UK and the US. This gives consumers &lt;strong&gt;better interest rates&lt;/strong&gt; and banks a &lt;strong&gt;diversified form of refinancing&lt;/strong&gt;. Our vision is to offer savings and investments without barriers and thus open up the global 160 trillion euro market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;sc-gEkIjz cjtSrT MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 sc-hoLEA&quot;&gt;Raisin currently employs more than 800 people from over 75 countries worldwide. Today, the platform holds over 80 billion euros in assets from&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;more than one million investors&lt;/strong&gt; which have accrued over 5 billion euros in returns.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;For further development and expansion of our successful business, Raisin is looking for a highly motivated, driven, and experienced &lt;strong&gt;Director of Engineering&lt;/strong&gt; to lead both strategically and operationally our Investment and Pension (IPP) teams (25+ engineers)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This embraces high-quality conceptual and delivery performance of the teams, the health of the IPP engineering organization and system landscape,&amp;nbsp; an efficient and compliant development process, technical and business ownership of the Raisin’s IPP platform, and vendor relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Raisin, we work in a domain driven organization with a binary-star leadership model. In this model, every Director of Engineering has a Product partner (Head of Product/ Director of Product).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director Engineering (DE) leads both strategically and operationally across multiple cross-functional teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This embraces the six impact areas (in details below):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivery quality and speed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team and culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process and compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Delivery quality and speed&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The DE is:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;accountable for fulfilling the agreed team commitments to their business-owners in time, scope, and budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;responsible for the performance of their teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;resolving impediments for their teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;nurturing a culture of accountability, pragmatism, and reusability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ensuring a strong delivery oriented collaboration between the different engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;leading both complex technical and important business projects&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;leading internal software engineering projects and initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The DE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;drives long-term value creation for their domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is fostering an environment of passion and fun for the business processes in their tribe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;builds resilient domain expertise in their teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;has a deep understanding of the existing system landscape of their teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;collaborates closely with their Business Owner and other stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;vendor management (evaluating, onboarding, and managing vendors)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tech Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The DE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;shapes the technical strategy for their teams according to the Raisin&#39;s business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;collaborates closely with other Sr. Engineering Leads in shaping and implementing Raisin&#39;s Tech Strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;actively initiates and contributes to strategic technical and architectural decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;is always considering the strategic benefits and price of:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;keeping an existing technical solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;introducing a new alternative (e.g framework, tech stack, tooling, process)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team and Culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The DE is:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;fully responsible for the health, resilience high performance, and development of their teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;offering direct leadership of engineering leads and sometimes also tech leads as well&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;encouraging accountability, creativity, risk-taking, and ownership by delegating responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;attracting, hiring, and retaining top technical talent for Raisin from around the world&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;proactively mentoring and coaching individual team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ensuring a strong delivery-oriented collaboration between the different engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;organizing workshops/hackathons&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;representing the company in external tech events advancing Raisin’s tech brand recognition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;shaping and driving knowledge transfer best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;nurturing and protecting our culture of trust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;initiating, owning and nurturing tech initiatives (like guilds, workshops, regular meetups)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;recognizing high performance and rewarding accomplishments within their teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process and Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The DE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;drives, improves, and applies existing Raisin standards and policies, regulation and data privacy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;contributes to an optimal toolchain with a high level of automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;develops, establishes, and continually improves documentation standards for the engineering organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;develops guidelines and best practices to ensure a lean software development process across different product teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;is responsible for the KPI-based reporting for their teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;actively monitors, analyses, and drives initiatives to continuously reduce their teams&#39; technical debt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;You hold a university degree in Computer Science,&amp;nbsp; Engineering, Information Systems, or related fields or have equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Leadership experience 10y+. You are a senior engineering leader, across projects and teams, with a natural aptitude and passion for growing and developing high-performing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have at least 4y experience in FinTech&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain knowledge of Investment products is a strong advantage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong business mindset&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Strong AWS knowledge, Java, SQL, Kafka or other messaging solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;You are pragmatic and can handle the balance between both taking and delegating the lead in challenging situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;You bring both strong strategic and excellent operational leadership skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;You motivate and inspire by outstanding communication and interpersonal skills, both written and verbal, including communicating technical concepts to non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;You possess solid engineering background and distinct hands-on mentality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;You are experienced with OKR and KPI-based target agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;You are familiar with architecturally-heavy systems, including designing, implementing, and evolving these system constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;You are fluent in English, knowledge of German or another European language would be a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join our mission, join our team – and grow with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Raisin, we care about each other and it is one of our top priorities to foster an open and caring environment in which everyone feels welcome and comfortable. Our culture is strongly driven by our ambitious team, which connects more than 75 different nationalities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of our team, you will benefit from:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Development Budget of €2,000 and four full training days per year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours, home office and 30 vacation days.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A company pension scheme (Betriebliche Altersvorsorge), which we support with 20%.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy more than 50+ different sports with Urban Sports Club: We subsidize your membership with more than €20 per month.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Do you miss being in the office? The Deutschland Ticket gets you there, which we subsidize with €25 per month.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Love cycling? With JobRad, lease the bike of your choice and enjoy tax savings, plus Raisin covers your monthly insurance costs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hungry all the time? Snacks, daily fresh fruit as well as drinks provided at the office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are moving from another country or city to join us? We may support your relocation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.raisin.com/corporate/raisin-applicant-privacy-policy/&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Raisin Applicant Privacy Policy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;728&quot; data-end=&quot;900&quot;&gt;We value diversity and the unique experiences each individual brings. If you’re excited about this role but don’t meet every requirement, we still encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;907&quot; data-end=&quot;1013&quot;&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for everyone, regardless of race, colour, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, or gender identity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Curious Minds. Bold Ideas. Extraordinary Impact&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re transforming financial services through bold innovation and relentless execution. You bring the ideas and drive. We&#39;ll build what&#39;s next — together.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Leads installations of technical systems, applications, or process designs for client’s purchased or outsourced technology and business process solutions. Senior member within team supporting clients with managing initial access, map, and transfer data, create process documentation, and train or coordinate training for client users. Troubleshoots complex client issues as they arise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Functions:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Capability to apply abstract reuse patterns to integrations and code both on platform and elsewhere using one or more nCino supported languages&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Ability to manipulate how Salesforce leverages, utilizes, and generates nCino supported languages&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Provide technical assistance and leadership for medium-to-large financial institutions and Implementation Service Consultants when building integrations into the nCino/Force.com platform using the nCino Integration Framework.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Begin to co-lead integrations from third-party systems into the nCino platform using any number of technical solutions based on the desired and proper approach for each unique project.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Document process and procedure to help streamline integration methodology.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Build and document testing requirements for unique projects.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Provide solution and integration development with Salesforce.com including requirements, functional specs, design, custom development, integration, testing and deployment.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Evaluate vendor API and interface specifications.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Handle multiple projects effectively while continuing to deliver exceptional quality.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Work independently and prioritize time and projects appropriately.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Translate customer requirements into implementation plans.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Drive customer success with a team player attitude.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Design a salesforce solution that meets the needs of the customer.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Effectively track time and bill for hours worked on customer projects.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Assist sales and sales engineering on technical prospect calls when required.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Leverage AI/ML capabilities to enhance integration frameworks, solution design, system automation, and operational efficiency.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Support the responsible use of AI-driven approaches in cloud-based solutions, DevOps practices, and Salesforce architecture to drive customer success and innovation.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Stay informed on emerging AI technologies and assist the team in identifying opportunities for scalable and secure AI integration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Typically requires a minimum of 8 years of related experience/ proficiency with a bachelor’s degree; or 6 years and a Master’s / Advanced degree; or equivalent work experience (as applicable). Some barriers to entry exist at this level, requiring department review.&#39;&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Ability to design, build, articulate and defend architectural designs, primarily around integrations, but including some basic UI components and designs&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Ability to support a dev ops process and build solutions with various software development practices&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Able to apply engineering principles to code, flow, and integration patterns including on and off platform tools&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Ability to document more complex solutions and customer facing documentation for work performed&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Salesforce Dev401 certification&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Strong research, analytical and creative problem-solving skills.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Advanced knowledge of data management, SQL and RDBMS technologies.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Experience using ETL/integration platforms&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Financial Services experience.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Experience with Salesforce.com developer toolkit IDE, Migration Tool, Web Services.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Exposure to Salesforce.com configuration and custom development.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Excellent understanding of object-oriented concepts and design patterns, as well as prior work with object-oriented languages&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Large FI experience, particularly with the Loan Origination/Servicing Systems, Enterprise Architecture framework&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Informatica experience.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Experience with Apex, SOQL, XML, JavaScript.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Salesforce System Architect.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Object-oriented languages such as Java, Ruby, C#, C++.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;ETL/integration platforms such as Cast Iron, Informatica, SnapLogic, etc.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Strong presentation and communication skills.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Strong customer and professional skills.&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Position may require some travel&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The pay range for this role is based on relative market data and alignment with our compensation philosophy. The range displayed reflects the minimum and maximum of the pay range for each job posting, which is used to determine new hire rates/salaries and takes into consideration multiple factors including but not limited to knowledge, skills, abilities, proficiencies, experience, education, &lt;span class=&quot;WGI1&quot;&gt;licensures/certifications,&lt;/span&gt; as well as business and organizational needs. nCino reserves the right to modify the posted range consistent with our internal practices and external market movement. The recruiter for this job posting can share more compensation details during the recruitment process, as base salary is only one component of the total compensation package per position posted.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The base salary range for this job is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€76.400&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€126.100 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;nCino provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, protected veteran status, disability, genetics or other protected groups. In addition to federal law requirements, nCino complies with applicable state and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment in every location in which the company has facilities. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, placement, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, transfer, leaves of absence, compensation and training.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;nCino is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. As part of this commitment, nCino will ensure that persons with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodations. If reasonable accommodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other benefits and privileges of employment, please contact us at &lt;a ----- -----
&lt;p&gt;Our commitment to inclusion and equality includes a strong belief that the diversity of our team is instrumental to our success.&amp;nbsp; We strive to create workplaces where employees are empowered to bring their authentic selves to work.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;_ymio1r31 _ypr0glyw _zcxs1o36 _mizu194a _1ah3dkaa _ra3xnqa1 _128mdkaa _1cvmnqa1 _4davt94y _4bfu18uv _1hms8stv _ajmmnqa1 _vchhusvi _kqswh2mm _ect4ttxp _2rkolb4i _syaz13af _1a3b18uv _4fpr8stv _5goinqa1 _f8pj13af _9oik18uv _1bnxglyw _jf4cnqa1 _30l313af _1nrm18uv _c2waglyw _1iohnqa1 _9h8h12zz _10531ra0 _1ien1ra0 _n0fx1ra0 _1vhv17z1&quot; href=&quot;https://www.ncino.com/ncino-applicant-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot; data-is-router-link=&quot;false&quot; data-testid=&quot;link-with-safety&quot;&gt;Please view our Applicant Privacy Policy here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

&lt;h2&gt;About Nscale&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nscale is the GPU cloud engineered for AI. We provide cost-effective, high-performance infrastructure for AI start-ups and large enterprise customers. Nscale enables AI-focused companies to achieve superior results by reducing the complexity of AI development. Our GPU cloud bolsters technical capabilities and directly supports strategic business outcomes, including cost management, rapid innovation, and environmental responsibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We thrive on a culture of relentless innovation, ownership, and accountability, where every team member takes pride in their work and drives it with excellence and urgency. As an Nscaler, you’ll build trust through openness and transparency, where everyone is inspired to do their best work. If you join our team, you’ll be contributing to building the technology that powers the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring an &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Infrastructure Engineer (OpenStack Ironic Specialist)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; to design, operate, and continuously improve the bare metal provisioning platforms that underpin Nscale’s infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits within the &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Infrastructure Engineering team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, which is responsible for the design, implementation, operation, and ongoing improvement of the infrastructure stack supporting both internal and customer-facing services. You’ll work closely with &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;network, compute, data centre, support, and pre-sales teams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, while also serving as a specialist escalation point for advanced provisioning and hardware issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact role focused on &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;OpenStack Ironic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, automated hardware lifecycle management, and the reliable operation of large-scale physical infrastructure. You’ll also help connect Nscale to the broader &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;upstream OpenStack community&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, ensuring our bare metal platforms evolve in line with real operational needs and industry direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Bare Metal Provisioning &amp;amp; Lifecycle Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; scalable and resilient bare metal provisioning platforms with a strong focus on &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;OpenStack Ironic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Own&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; the full lifecycle of physical infrastructure, including discovery, enrolment, provisioning, cleaning, deprovisioning, and hardware state management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Build&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and maintain provisioning workflows for a wide range of hardware profiles, including &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;GPU-enabled&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and high-performance server platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; platform upgrades, lifecycle management, and operational improvements across &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Ironic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and its dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Automation &amp;amp; Platform Integration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Manage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and improve integrations between &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Ironic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and related OpenStack services such as &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Nova, Neutron, Glance, Keystone, and Placement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Drive&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; automation for hardware onboarding, firmware and BIOS configuration, deployment workflows, validation, and recovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Implement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; infrastructure automation using &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;infrastructure-as-code&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and configuration management approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Ensure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; provisioning platforms and operational processes align with security, compliance, and operational standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Troubleshooting, Reliability &amp;amp; Operational Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Troubleshoot&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; complex issues across provisioning pipelines, &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;PXE/iPXE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, BMC interfaces, out-of-band management, image deployment, network boot, and hardware compatibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Act&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; as a &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;3rd/4th line escalation point&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; for advanced bare metal and provisioning incidents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Perform&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; root cause analysis and implement long-term fixes to improve platform reliability and repeatability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Participate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; in on-call rotations and incident response activities for critical infrastructure services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration &amp;amp; Community Engagement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Collaborate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; with network, compute, data centre, and support teams to deliver reliable physical infrastructure services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Contribute&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; specialist input to infrastructure roadmap planning, capacity expansion, standard builds, and hardware platform qualification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; pre-sales and solution design efforts with expert guidance on bare metal capabilities, operational models, and deployment constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Contribute&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; to upstream OpenStack bare metal communities through bug reports, testing, reviews, design discussions, and code contributions where appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Track&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; upstream roadmaps and release changes to help shape Nscale’s bare metal strategy, upgrade planning, and platform standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;KPIs&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Automated provisioning and hardware onboarding reliability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Bare metal incident resolution and root cause closure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Platform upgrade and lifecycle delivery across Ironic dependencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Upstream OpenStack Ironic community contribution and adoption alignment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About You&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Strong experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; operating Linux systems and troubleshooting production infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Strong specialist knowledge&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; of &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;OpenStack Ironic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and the surrounding provisioning ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Strong understanding&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; of bare metal provisioning concepts including &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;PXE/iPXE, DHCP, TFTP/HTTP boot, BMC technologies, RAID configuration, firmware management, disk imaging, and node lifecycle states&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Strong experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; with out-of-band management technologies such as &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Redfish, IPMI, or vendor management interfaces&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Strong experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; designing and building automation for physical and virtual infrastructure using tools such as &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Ansible&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;6&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Strong scripting skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; in &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Python and Bash&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;7&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; troubleshooting complex provisioning and hardware integration issues across server, network, and management layers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;8&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; operating infrastructure at scale with a focus on reliability, repeatability, and operational safety&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Ability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; to collaborate across infrastructure, support, and architecture teams to solve complex technical problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;10&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; contributing to or working closely with upstream open-source communities, particularly &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;OpenStack, Ironic, Metal3, or related infrastructure projects&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, is highly desirable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we can offer you&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Nscale, you&#39;ll find a collaborative, supportive, and innovative environment where your contributions spark real impact. We&#39;re building something extraordinary, and we want you at the core.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Highly competitive US compensation package (base + bonus + equity), with performance reviews every 12 months. 🚀&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join one of the fastest-growing AI infrastructure companies — your chance to directly shape how global AI capacity is planned and deployed. ✨&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Expect a dynamic progression plan tailored to your ambitions. Grow by leading critical cross-functional initiatives and shaping capital strategy — always with our full support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Human-First Flexibility: We treat you as humans first. 🫶🏽 Our flexible workplace trusts Nscalers to deliver, giving you the autonomy to shape your day around life&#39;s moments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Equal Opportunities Statement&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We strongly encourage applications from people of colour, the LGBTQ+ community, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, parents, carers, and people from lower socio-economic backgrounds.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If there’s anything we can do to accommodate your specific situation, please let us know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The responsibilities outlined in this job description are not exhaustive and are intended to provide a general overview of the position. The employee may be required to perform additional duties, tasks, and responsibilities as assigned by management, consistent with the skills and qualifications required for the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For information on how Nscale handles candidate personal data, please see our Employee &amp;amp; Candidate Privacy Notice: Here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For information on how Nscale handles candidate personal data, please see our Employee &amp;amp; Candidate Privacy Notice: Here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Salary Range&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The range below reflects the base salary for the position. Actual compensation may vary based on job-related factors such as skill set, experience, education, and location. In addition to base salary, this role may be eligible for bonus, equity, and/or commission programs. Nscale may offer a competitive benefits package including medical, dental, vision, flexible paid time off, parental leave, and retirement plan participation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For information on how Nscale handles candidate personal data, please see our Employee &amp;amp; Candidate Privacy Notice:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://drive.google.com/file/d/1QK5Yg04WHD9K9IAtJgQWubJZC9oLvatK/view?usp=sharing&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://drive.google.com/file/d/1QK5Yg04WHD9K9IAtJgQWubJZC9oLvatK/view?usp%3Dsharing&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1765375172804000&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw2Ncte4rmlGl8OKuFuDgDtx&quot;&gt;Here.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nscale does not accept unsolicited candidate submissions from recruitment agencies.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;gmail_default&quot; style=&quot;font-size: small;&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Mozilla?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Mozilla Corporation is the non-profit-backed technology company that has shaped the internet for the better over the last 25 years. We make pioneering brands like Firefox, the privacy-minded web browser. Now, with more than 225 million people around the world using our products each month, we’re shaping the next 25 years of technology and helping to reclaim an internet built for people, not companies. Our work focuses on diverse areas including AI, social media, security and more. And we’re doing this while never losing our focus on our core mission – to make the internet better for people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The Mozilla Corporation is wholly owned by the non-profit 501(c) Mozilla Foundation. This means we aren’t beholden to any shareholders — only to our mission. Along with thousands of volunteer contributors and collaborators all over the world, Mozillians design, build and distribute &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;open-source&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; software that enables people to enjoy the internet on their terms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design, build and implement security and hardening features for enterprise users:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Design, implement, test, and ship cutting-edge security features that strengthen Firefox’s security posture.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advance Firefox’s security architecture across multiple operating systems: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Contribute to and drive cutting-edge improvements to Firefox’s core security posture, by building privilege isolation and moving trust boundaries &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;or Strengthen Firefox’s security architecture:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Improve Firefox’s core security mechanisms including cryptographic protocols, WebPKI, and security-sensitive web APIs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribute to our security initiatives:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Work across teams to investigate security issues, identify root causes, and deliver robust, maintainable fixes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improve browser reliability and performance:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Diagnose and resolve issues affecting stability, correctness, performance, and memory usage in a complex, multithreaded environment.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems programming experience and security knowledge:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; 3+ years of experience in low-level software engineering, strong proficiency in C and/or C++, and a solid understanding of security fundamentals.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Debugging and problem-solving skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Experience diagnosing and resolving issues in multithreaded, cross-platform native applications, including memory and performance challenges.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Web platform and modern systems experience: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Familiarity with web technologies (HTML, CSS, JavaScript) and interest or experience in Rust; ability to work effectively within large, complex, multi-language codebases.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Effective collaboration and communication:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Experience working with distributed teams and communicating technical ideas clearly in writing and conversation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll get:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Generous performance-based bonus plans to all eligible employees - we share in our success as one team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Generous retirement contributions with 100% immediate vesting (regardless of whether you contribute)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Quarterly all-company wellness days where everyone takes a pause together&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Country specific holidays plus a day off for your birthday&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;One-time home office stipend&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Annual professional development budget&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Quarterly well-being stipend&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Considerable paid parental leave&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Employee referral bonus program&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Other benefits (life/AD&amp;amp;D, disability, EAP, etc. - varies by country)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Mozilla&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mozilla exists to build the Internet as a public resource accessible to all because we believe that open and free is better than closed and controlled. When you work at Mozilla, you give yourself a chance to make a difference in the lives of Web users everywhere. And you give us a chance to make a difference in your life every single day. Join us to work on the Web as the platform and help create more opportunity and innovation for everyone online.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mozilla understands that valuing diverse creative practices and forms of knowledge are crucial to and enrich the company’s core mission.&amp;nbsp; We encourage applications from everyone, including members of all equity-seeking communities, such as (but certainly not limited to) women, racialized and Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, persons of all sexual orientation&lt;span style=&quot;color: #003366;&quot;&gt;s, &lt;/span&gt;gender identities, and expressions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We will ensure that qualified individuals with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodations to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and to receive other benefits and privileges of employment, as appropriate. Please contact us at &lt;a class=&quot;external-link&quot; ---------- to request accommodation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate on the basis of race (including hairstyle and texture), religion (including religious grooming and dress practices), gender, gender identity, gender expression, color, national origin, pregnancy, ancestry, domestic partner status, disability, sexual orientation, age, genetic predisposition, medical condition, marital status, citizenship status, military or veteran status, or any other basis covered by applicable laws.&amp;nbsp; Mozilla will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics or any other unlawful behavior, conduct, or purpose.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Group: D&lt;/p&gt;
