&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Liftoff offers a fast-paced, collaborative, and innovative work environment where employees are empowered to grow and make an impact. We’re shaping the future of the mobile app ecosystem—join us and help accelerate what’s next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Liftoff’s compensation strategy includes competitive salaries, equity, and benefits designed to support employee well-being and performance. We benchmark compensation based on role, level, and location to ensure fairness and market alignment. Benefits may include medical coverage, wellness stipends, and additional perks based on your country of residence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Liftoff is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees and applicants regardless of race, ethnicity, national origin, age, marital status, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agency and Third Party Recruiter Notice:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Liftoff does not accept unsolicited resumes from individual recruiters or third-party recruiting agencies in response to job postings. No fee will be paid to third parties who submit unsolicited candidates directly to our hiring managers or Recruiting Team. All candidates must be submitted via our Applicant Tracking System by approved Liftoff vendors who have been expressly requested to make a submission by our Recruiting Team for a specific job opening. No placement fees will be paid to any firm unless such a request has been made by the Liftoff Recruiting Team and such a candidate was submitted to the Liftoff Recruiting Team via our Applicant Tracking System.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

Established in 2004, OLIVER is the world's first and only specialist in designing, building, and running bespoke in-house agencies and marketing ecosystems for brands. We partner with over 300 clients in 40+ countries and counting. Our unique model drives creativity and efficiency, allowing us to deliver tailored solutions that resonate deeply with audiences.&nbsp;
As a part of The Brandtech Group, we're at the forefront of leveraging cutting-edge AI technology to revolutionise how we create and deliver work. Our AI solutions enhance efficiency, spark creativity, and drive insightful decision-making, empowering our teams to produce innovative and impactful results.&nbsp;Role: Director of Social &amp; Creator – Dove Social Studios
Location: London (Global remit), 2–3 days per week 
The Opportunity:
The&nbsp;role is on the Dove Social Studio, an always-on content &amp; social engine spanning 15 markets. It drives social-first excellence for one of the world's most iconic, purposeful brands, connecting Dove's values with audiences through culture, creativity &amp; community.&nbsp;
This is an opportunity to shape how Dove connects with millions of people globally &amp; define best-in-class social for both the brand &amp; the industry.&nbsp;
About the role:&nbsp;
As Director of Social &amp; Creators, you will set the global standard for how Dove shows up on social &amp; inspire a multi-market team to continually raise the bar.&nbsp;
Sitting on the client Global Leadership Team, you'll define how one of the world's most iconic brands shows up on social — and lead the multi-market team that delivers it. You'll oversee social media managers, creator leads, and senior social experts across markets, building capability, setting standards, and driving a programme that is native to platform, culture, and audience. As the senior social adviser to the client's global team, you'll translate platform expertise into confident, clear strategic direction.
What you will be doing:&nbsp;
Social Platform Leadership

Define global social frameworks, standards, and best practice across client Social Studios
Identify platform opportunities, cultural moments, and emerging formats — and translate them into clear strategic action
Act as the studio's social authority, championing platform-native thinking across creative and content output

Creator &amp; Influencer Strategy

Own the client's end-to-end creator and influence programme — from strategy design through to delivery
Evolve the programme in line with audience behaviour, platform developments, and brand values
Oversee creator managers and a large UGC network, maintaining creative quality, brand alignment, and scalable delivery
Coordinate creator activity across markets and ensure consistent use of the Creator Bench

Team Leadership &amp; Capability

Lead and develop a global, multi-disciplinary team of social media managers, creator managers, and senior social experts
Set clear objectives and build a culture of curiosity, craft, and continuous improvement
Coach talent at all levels; create visible pathways for professional growth

Client Partnership

Serve as the primary social-craft partner to senior client stakeholders globally
Translate platform expertise and audience insight into strategic counsel, platform reviews, and brand presentations
Build trusted relationships with senior stakeholders, operating credibly at global marketing director level and above

Content &amp; Campaign Planning

Put social insight, audience behaviour, and platform understanding at the centre of content and campaign planning
Set community management standards that consistently reflect the client's voice, values, and purpose

Commercial &amp; Budget Accountability

Oversee studio-level and creator programme budgets; present financial performance to client and OLIVER senior stakeholders
Drive cost-effective delivery across a multi-market creator ecosystem — balancing quality, scale, and commercial health
Accountable for the financial health of the social and creator discipline within the studio

What you need to be great in this role:&nbsp;

Extensive social media leadership experience in a large brand, agency or hybrid environment, working across multiple markets&nbsp;


Deep expertise across major &amp; emerging social platforms, with a strong understanding of the evolving landscape&nbsp;


Proven experience leading creator strategy &amp; managing large creator ecosystems&nbsp;


Strong people leadership &amp; senior client skills, with the credibility to operate at the highest levels&nbsp;


Operational rigour &amp; the ability to bring clarity to complex, multi-market programmes&nbsp;

Gen AI &amp; Agentic Thinking&nbsp;

Use Gen AI tools to improve ideation, listening, trend detection, creator sourcing &amp; community workflows without compromising craft&nbsp;


Set quality standards, brand-safety guardrails &amp; best practice for responsible AI use&nbsp;


Critically assess AI-generated work for cultural nuance, brand fit &amp; human judgement&nbsp;


Build AI literacy across teams &amp; explain its role credibly to clients &amp; senior stakeholders&nbsp;

Why This Role&nbsp;
You will work alongside brilliant, driven people who care deeply about the work, the brand &amp; each other, with the freedom to define best-in-class social for one of the world's most loved brands.&nbsp;
As part of The Brandtech Group, the social studio uses technology &amp; AI to enhance creative work while protecting craft, inclusion &amp; responsible practice. We are pro-inclusive &amp; anti-racist across our community, clients &amp; work. If you are excited by the role but do not meet every requirement, we encourage you to apply. We support flexible working &amp; reasonable adjustments throughout the process.&nbsp;
