&lt;h2 class=&quot;entry-intro&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;entry-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;iframe src=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/embed/djJ0q6231tI?feature=shared&quot; width=&quot;560&quot; height=&quot;314&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;entry-intro&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;entry-intro&quot;&gt;In a nutshell&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;group/conversation-turn relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn&quot; style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;flex-col gap-1 md:gap-3&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;flex max-w-full flex-col flex-grow&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;min-h-[20px] text-message flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 whitespace-normal break-words [.text-message+&amp;amp;]:mt-5&quot; data-message-author-role=&quot;assistant&quot; data-message-id=&quot;266e3a10-dc9a-4829-b84e-6cf8d3c0f2e0&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert light&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Recruitment team plays a crucial role in finding top talent worldwide and persuading them to join Picnic. If you have excellent communication skills, thrive on identifying the right profiles, and know how to get candidates excited about unique challenges, we want to hear from you! Understanding the profiles we seek is key, as finding the right people is vital to our success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will take full ownership of your fulfilling roles, organize recruitment initiatives and source the best talent out there. If you are proactive, solution-driven and excited to grow our business, we’d love to meet you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is &lt;strong&gt;not &lt;/strong&gt;a support role - it’s an entry point into Talent Acquisition. Our goal is to build a lasting partnership. We’re eager to consider high-performing interns for full-time roles to continue shaping Picnic&#39;s future together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Tricks of the trade&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;: You&#39;ll work closely with our recruiters and various internal teams to understand the specific requirements for open positions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sourcing&lt;/strong&gt;: Using LinkedIn Search and other search techniques, you&#39;ll actively look for potential candidates and approach them to explore opportunities at Picnic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;: You will design and execute creative strategies to build robust talent pipelines, taking full ownership of the search for unique talent while aligning with broader team goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation&lt;/strong&gt;: You&#39;ll bring fresh ideas and provide valuable input to enhance our talent pipeline processes and improve overall recruitment outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For example, every year at Picnic we organize a Business Course event for potential Analyst candidates (see video &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AyQh6HZ_Pgo&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;). In 2026, it could be YOU the one recruiting for it, together with the support of our colleagues.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Your superpowers&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are currently enrolled in a Master’s programma in Psychology, HRM, Business Administration or similar fields&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have prior internships or working-student experience, preferably in active sourcing or recruiting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills in English and German&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are available for 40 hrs p/w, for a minimum of 4 months&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have EU citizenship (mandatory)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Note: this is a regular internship opportunity (no thesis internship or project internship)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Picnic, we use Greenhouse as our ATS. It&#39;s great if you&#39;re familiar with it or if you&#39;re curious to learn!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Picnic Perks&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;section vacancy-detail-info-section&quot;&gt;🚀&lt;strong&gt;Every expert was once a beginner!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;You’ll get plenty of opportunities to challenge yourself and grow, including Lunch &amp;amp; Learn sessions, and tailored soft skills training.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;section vacancy-detail-info-section&quot;&gt;&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;section vacancy-detail-info-section&quot;&gt;🌍&lt;strong&gt;Make a difference&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;You’ll work in an awesome startup environment with the freedom to drive your own projects and create a visible impact. Our fully electric vehicles and sustainable business model mean you’ll also be contributing to making the world a better place!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;section vacancy-detail-info-section&quot;&gt;&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;section vacancy-detail-info-section&quot;&gt;🤝&lt;strong&gt;Teamwork makes the dream work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;With more than 80 nationalities across 3 countries, you’ll be part of a diverse company with plenty of cool stuff to get involved with, from board game evenings to after-work drinks to our company ski trip and more!&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;section vacancy-detail-info-section&quot;&gt;&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;section vacancy-detail-info-section&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🥗Fresh Lunch, coffee, and snacks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;section vacancy-detail-info-section&quot;&gt;Our offices are equipped with fully-fledged coffee bars and a kitchen and chefs. They prepare delicious fresh and warm lunches every day so you can keep your energy up.&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;section vacancy-detail-info-section&quot;&gt;&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;section vacancy-detail-info-section&quot;&gt;💪&lt;strong&gt;Stay healthy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Mental health is important. As well as having the option to speak with Picnic colleagues who act as confidential advisors, our collaboration with OpenUp gives you easy access to professional psychologists, along with workshops and materials.&lt;br&gt;There are plenty of sports communities and events to get involved with, from tennis to yoga to climbing!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;section vacancy-detail-info-section&quot;&gt;&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;section vacancy-detail-info-section&quot;&gt;💰&lt;strong&gt;Attractive package&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We offer €800 per month gross salary for a full-time internship, along with a laptop and phone to support your work. Travel costs can also be reimbursed, depending on your location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;Find Jobs in Netherlands on Arbeitnow

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Sony Music Entertainment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Sony Music Entertainment, we fuel the creative journey. We’ve played a pioneering role in music history, from the first-ever music label to the invention of the flat disc record. We’ve nurtured some of music’s most iconic artists and produced some of the most influential recordings of all time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today, we work in more than 70 countries, supporting a diverse roster of international superstars, developing and independent artists, and visionary creators. From our position at the intersection of music, entertainment, and technology, we bring imagination and expertise to the newest products and platforms, embrace new business models, employ breakthrough tools, and provide powerful insights that help our artists push creative boundaries and reach new audiences. In everything we do, we’re committed to artistic integrity, transparency, and entrepreneurship.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sony Music Entertainment is a member of the Sony family of global companies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sony Music is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Product Manager, Data &lt;/strong&gt;to join our talented product team in our London office and lead the development of a portfolio of shared data products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our products and teams work with data spanning streaming, fan engagement, social and creator activity, and commerce. As new datasets and requirements emerge, we need to understand what the data contains, establish what it means and make it useful beyond the team or product where it originated.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own the strategy, roadmap and delivery of a portfolio of shared data products. Working with business stakeholders, source-product owners and data engineering, you will turn business needs into clear requirements, deliver dependable datasets and establish definitions and relationships that can be reused across products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the strategy and roadmap for a portfolio of shared data products, with a focus on developing new datasets to meet emerging business needs.&lt;/strong&gt; Understand needs across teams, identify valuable opportunities and prioritise a portfolio of initiatives that supports artist teams and the wider business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Turn business requests into well-defined data initiatives.&lt;/strong&gt; Meet the people who produce and use the data, examine source datasets and establish the questions users need to answer, the information required and the measures of success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define reusable datasets with engineering.&lt;/strong&gt; Agree on the records, fields, relationships, quality, freshness and access requirements needed for each use case you’re defining. Establish clear acceptance criteria and resolve tradeoffs with stakeholders and engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead delivery and adoption.&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain a prioritised backlog and work with engineering through implementation, validation, launch and ongoing improvement. Ensure the teams receiving the data can use it to meet the agreed need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Steward shared definitions and data models.&lt;/strong&gt; Work with domain experts and engineers to establish consistent definitions, identifiers, relationships and metrics. Develop the shared semantic layer through the initiatives you deliver, so concepts such as artists, tracks, markets, campaigns and audiences can be understood consistently across products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Connect datasets to enable new capabilities.&lt;/strong&gt; Identify where combining data creates value and lead the product work required, including opportunities to relate streaming performance to social activity, campaigns, fan engagement and commerce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make data discoverable and understandable.&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure data products have clear documentation, usage examples and known limitations, helping analysts, data scientists and downstream product teams use them confidently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Help develop and apply practical data standards.&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with leadership, engineering and relevant specialists on quality, ownership, access, lineage and appropriate use. Translate these expectations into requirements for the data products you lead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agree responsibilities for ongoing use of the data products you deliver.&lt;/strong&gt; Work with source-product owners and engineering teams to establish how source changes, maintenance, quality issues and communication with users will be handled for those initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measure adoption and impact.&lt;/strong&gt; Gather user feedback and evidence of usefulness, track whether the capabilities delivered meet their intended outcomes and use those findings to inform the roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build stakeholder alignment.&lt;/strong&gt; Explain priorities and investment decisions, communicate progress and translate technical considerations into clear business implications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with our existing Data Platform product and engineering teams, coordinating priorities and dependencies with the platform migration and operational roadmap. You will also partner with source-product PMs and the teams building on the shared data products you deliver.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a track record of leading data products or platform capabilities from discovery and strategy through delivery, adoption and ongoing improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can set a clear product direction and prioritise pragmatically, balancing business value, user needs, technical constraints and dependencies across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable examining source data and working through detailed requirements with business experts, analysts and engineers..&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience turning fragmented data and business requirements into reusable datasets, shared capabilities or data products that support multiple use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong understanding of modern data platforms, including Snowflake or comparable cloud data warehouses, and can work effectively with engineers on data ingestion, modelling, pipelines and downstream consumption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand semantic layers and shared data definitions, and can work with business and technical partners to establish consistent meaning across products and domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can make informed product decisions about data quality, freshness, ownership, access and lineage, with an understanding of privacy and appropriate data use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable working across product boundaries, clarifying responsibilities and influencing teams whose roadmaps and priorities may differ.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong analytical and organisational skills, with the ability to translate complex problems into clear requirements, priorities and delivery plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate effectively with technical teams, business stakeholders and executives, creating alignment around both the work and the outcomes it should deliver.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong documentation skills and can make data products, definitions and decisions understandable to the teams that depend on them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You focus on whether people can use and rely on the capabilities you deliver, with experience measuring adoption, usefulness and business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in the music or entertainment industry, particularly with streaming, consumption or artist audience data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with fan engagement, social and creator analytics, marketing campaigns, D2C commerce or customer data platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience connecting data across platforms through shared identifiers, entity relationships or audience segmentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building data capabilities that support analytics, marketing intelligence or AI-powered products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data catalogs, observability tools or business intelligence platforms such as Sigma.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing global or enterprise-scale data products, platform migrations or change management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we give you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You join a vibrant global community with the opportunity to channel your passion every day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A modern office environment designed for you, empowering you to bring your best.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investment in your professional growth and development enabling you to thrive in our vibrant community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The space to accelerate progress, positively disrupt and create what happens next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We give you the platform to champion positive change, with the opportunity to contribute to our social impact, diversity, equity and inclusion initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We provide an excellent range of benefits like private medical cover, a generous pension scheme, life assurance, income protection, plus loads of music industry perks. There’s also time off over winter break.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an active part of a culturally and socially diverse society, Sony Music’s aim is that our workforce is diverse and inclusive. Sony Music is an equal opportunity employer and supports workforce diversity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We employ, retain, promote and otherwise treat all employees and job applicants according to their merit, qualifications, competence and talent. We apply this policy without regard to any individual’s sex, race, religion, origin, age, sexual orientation, marital status, medical condition or disability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please click&lt;a href=&quot;http://tools.sonymusiccreative.com/privacy/PCP_UK.pdf&quot;&gt; here&lt;/a&gt; to read our privacy policy before beginning the application process as you will need to agree to the terms of the policy before submitting your information. &lt;strong&gt;Please note that applicants must be at least 18 years of age&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At NiCE, we don’t limit our challenges. We challenge our limits. Always. We’re ambitious. We’re game changers. And we play to win. We set the highest standards and execute beyond them. And if you’re like us, we can offer you the ultimate career opportunity that will light a fire within you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position: Technical Product Owner&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: Hedge End, Hampshire&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;So, what’s the role all about?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here at NiCE Public Safety, we develop state of the art solutions for the Public Safety market, bringing together voice, video and screen recording, playback and analysis for Security customers worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are currently expanding our development team to allow us to continue to develop an exciting product that enables Police forces worldwide to keep up with the increasing demands of managing growing amounts of digital evidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;How will you make an impact?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You own the Product Plan, driven from the Product roadmap, created by the Product Managers&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You create a prioritised backlog based on High Level product requirements&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You work closely with NICE Architects and Product Managers to clearly describe business goals and customer requirements into product backlog items&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Assess and review technical documentation and ensure the development team create appropriate levels of product documentation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You support the Product Manager in development of user scenarios for technical users&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You work closely with R&amp;amp;D to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Explain the motivation and the customer needs behind a new requirement&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own and Groom (create and explain) the User stories&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Be there daily for the team for any questions &amp;amp; feedback&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Understand and prioritise technical requirements&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Somebody who’s comfortable getting into a detailed technical discussion with our team of software developers&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Happy to work on back-end solutions (e.g. software running as Windows Services)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You provide support to Customer Support, Professional Services, Technical Pre-sales teams and Training where required&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Have you got what it takes?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bachelor’s degree in a technical discipline/STEM subject, preferably Computer Science or Engineering, MBA&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to multitask and prioritise work&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to understand technical solutions, experience of software development&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to understand the big picture and translate it to detailed needs&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience working in an Agile delivery methodology organisation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Communicating effectively at all levels, from executive management to individual contributor&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Excellent English verbal and writing communication skills&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fast learner with ability to educate her/himself on relevant technologies e.g. Azure / Cloud-based services&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to remain focused and calm under pressure&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Great interpersonal skills&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;You will have an advantage if you also have:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
